","label":"Original Audio"}]},{"id":"1410599508492305488","title":"White as Snow","type":"movie","category":"movies","year":"2019","poster":"https://pbcdn.aoneroom.com/image/2026/01/26/9db9a6b181083519e7236ef1fa8cefba.jpg","description":"Claire works at her late father's hotel run by evil stepmother Maud. Maud's lover falls for Claire, sparking jealousy. Maud plots against Claire who finds refuge on a farm with \"seven princes,\" breaking free from her strict upbringing.","rating":"5.4","director":null,"cast":null,"genres":null,"duration":"1h 52m","season_count":0,"streams":[{"quality":"360p","url":"https://bcdn.hakunaymatata.com/resource/db5a9cb2a5bb4e8394fa43494bc3e63e.mp4?sign=46c6111f0c5dfba33218f498b09cc142&t=1795691976","format":"mp4","codec":"h264","size":"394571954","season":null,"episode":0},{"quality":"480p","url":"https://bcdn.hakunaymatata.com/resource/8fff221af6c42d8d6df2e7edb14cfd03.mp4?sign=969993f611e0c1dbea0fff98f230197d&t=1795691976","format":"mp4","codec":"h264","size":"506149799","season":null,"episode":0},{"quality":"720p","url":"https://bcdn.hakunaymatata.com/resource/4df848ef0a9bee3a1d6fef02a3ff0f0a.mp4?sign=df6b6cc9ca43e60620125c2f945da5e1&t=1795691976","format":"mp4","codec":"h264","size":"609879582","season":null,"episode":0},{"quality":"360p","url":"https://bcdn4.hakunaymatata.com/resource/db5a9cb2a5bb4e8394fa43494bc3e63e.mp4?sign=46c6111f0c5dfba33218f498b09cc142&t=1795691976","format":"mp4","codec":"h264","size":"394571954","headers":{"Referer":"https://sportslive.wine","User-Agent":"com.community.oneroom/50020119 (Linux; U; Android 11; en_US; M2007J20CG; Build/RP1A.200720.011; Cronet/135.0.7012.3)"},"season":null,"episode":null},{"quality":"480p","url":"https://bcdn4.hakunaymatata.com/resource/8fff221af6c42d8d6df2e7edb14cfd03.mp4?sign=969993f611e0c1dbea0fff98f230197d&t=1795691976","format":"mp4","codec":"h264","size":"506149799","headers":{"Referer":"https://sportslive.wine","User-Agent":"com.community.oneroom/50020119 (Linux; U; Android 11; en_US; M2007J20CG; Build/RP1A.200720.011; Cronet/135.0.7012.3)"},"season":null,"episode":null},{"quality":"360p","url":"https://bcdn.hakunaymatata.com/resource/db5a9cb2a5bb4e8394fa43494bc3e63e.mp4?sign=f8e097ae7b83d8e7f6f86d604f03c2cf&t=1795691643","format":"mp4","codec":"h264","size":"394571954","season":null,"episode":0},{"quality":"480p","url":"https://bcdn.hakunaymatata.com/resource/8fff221af6c42d8d6df2e7edb14cfd03.mp4?sign=9a5682057795d5b5977c8cc29de61885&t=1795691643","format":"mp4","codec":"h264","size":"506149799","season":null,"episode":0},{"quality":"720p","url":"https://bcdn.hakunaymatata.com/resource/4df848ef0a9bee3a1d6fef02a3ff0f0a.mp4?sign=27cc8610958b0d027469624f2e92d5ea&t=1795691643","format":"mp4","codec":"h264","size":"609879582","season":null,"episode":0}],"episodes":[],"dubs":[{"subject_id":"1410599508492305488","language":"Original Audio","label":"Original Audio"},{"subject_id":"4797615611159479784","language":"Hindi dub","label":"Hindi dub"}]},{"id":"6809588852303741624","title":"As Husbands Go","type":"movie","category":"movies","year":"1934","poster":"https://pbcdn.aoneroom.com/image/2023/08/09/3c857e7719c7ac777c18497fb2866102.jpg","description":"On their last night in Paris, Lucille Lingard and her traveling companion, widow Emmie Sykes, are squired around town by their new European gentleman acquaintances, Ronald Derbyshire and Hippolitus \"Hippy\" Lomi. The two are upset because they must leave their newly acquired Continental friends for their Dubuque, Iowa homes. On their voyage home, Lucille complains to Emmie that her good-natured, though boring, Midwestern husband is no match for the charming and sophisticated Ronald, whom she left behind. Emmie, who is older than Lucille, her daughter Peggy and Peggy's fiance, Jake Canon, all live with Lucille and her family. Emmie is distressed that she has been unable to get her daughter to approve of her new relationship with Hippy. Despite their commitments at home, both women had promised their European lovers to return to them some day, and Lucille had promised Ronald to divorce her husband. Lucille and Emmie make a pact to pursue their new goals without distraction. While crossing the Atlantic, Lucille and Emmie unexpectedly receive word that Hippy and Ronald plan to follow them to America. Meanwhile, Charles makes special preparations for his wife's return by adopting his nephew Wilbur into the Lingard family. Lucille arrives in Dubuque but shows nothing but disdain for her husbands's bland Midwestern lifestyle and longs for a return to Ronald. When Ronald and Hippy arrive, Charles senses that Ronald is interested in Emmie, not realizing he has come for Lucille. As Charles and Ronald get to know each other, however, they become fast friends and get drunk on a fishing expedition. In their drunken chatter, Ronald admits to Charles that Lucille does not look as glamorous to him in America as she did in Europe, and confesses that he is really too selfish to love a woman the same way Charles does. Meanwhile, Peggy's heart softens about her mother's love for Hippy, and she realizes Emmie is truly happy with him. The next day Lucille is told that Ronald has left, and she happily returns to her husband, finally realizing the value of their marriage and the joy her new family will bring to her.","rating":null,"director":null,"cast":null,"genres":null,"duration":"1h 18m","season_count":0,"streams":[],"episodes":[],"dubs":[]},{"id":"8095282759696008016","title":"As Bicicletas & a Cidade","type":"movie","category":"movies","year":"2017","poster":"https://pbcdn.aoneroom.com/image/2023/08/13/cb269cd4280b1e06fe240f7bd0ffb0ab.jpg","description":"During the 20th century, the city of Joinville, southern Brazil, experienced a phase of intense industrialization, receiving migrants in search of work. During this period, bicycles became the main means of transport for the population, making Joinville known as the \"City of Bicycles. But this title did not last forever!\n\nBased on photographs, newspaper articles and tax records on bicycles - as the first bicycles were called - found in the Joinville Historical Archive, the document shows how different phases of bicycle use in the city are. Among the anonymous and known, complement the approach, testimonies of researchers such as the geographer Naum Alves Santanna, the historian Dilney Cunha, the coordinator of the Bicycle Museum Valter Bustos, the researcher Dietmar Lilie of the Movimento Pedala Joinville, and people who use a bicycle Joinville in other times, such as retired worker and cycling champion Renato Saramento, researcher Jutta Haggemann, artist Juarez Machado, retired workers Frida Rudin and Heinzi Gnewuch, among others.\n\nCreator, screenwriter and director of the documentary, the fellow Fellipe Giesel, with cameras attached to the interviewees themselves, recorded the subjective view of those who currently use the bicycle in Joinville. \"Bicycles and the City\" brings, for those who do not ride, a sample of the difficulties that cyclists are going through (including wheelchair users) and leaves questions about these problems. The documentary is his first feature film and was made with sponsorship from the Municipality and the Cultural Foundation of Joinville through the Municipal System for Development through Culture (Simdec).","rating":null,"director":null,"cast":null,"genres":null,"duration":"1h 22m","season_count":0,"streams":[],"episodes":[],"dubs":[]},{"id":"5389587177217084352","title":"As Man Made Her","type":"movie","category":"movies","year":"1917","poster":"https://pbcdn.aoneroom.com/image/2023/08/09/4c2e3a73cbf8d23f095311e2347f8e80.jpg","description":"After graduating from finishing school, Claire Wilson falls into the hands of wealthy rake Mason Forbes. After installing her as his mistress, Mason abandons Claire to marry socialite Grace Hughes. Out of revenge, Grace marries Harold, Mason's younger brother and the two couples live together under one roof. 